meta {
  name: Create Quote Recap (Missing Month)
  type: http
  seq: 12
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/quote-recaps
  body: json
  auth: inherit
}

headers {
  Content-Type: application/json
  ~X-Branch-Id: {{branchId}}
}

body:json {
  {
    "leadId": "{{createdLeadId}}",
    "policies": [
      { "policyType": "Auto", "premium": 1200.00, "itemCount": 1 }
    ],
    "quoteDocument": {
      "key": "{{quoteDocumentKey}}",
      "filename": "carrier-quote.pdf",
      "contentType": "application/pdf",
      "size": 2048
    }
  }
}

tests {
  test("rejects a create with no renewal month", function () {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(400);
  });

  test("names the field, so the form can point at it", function () {
    const body = res.getBody();
    expect(body).to.have.property("errors");
    expect(JSON.stringify(body.errors)).to.contain("insuranceRenewalMonth");
  });

  test("no submissionToken, so nothing was created to clean up", function () {
    expect(res.getBody()).to.not.have.property("id");
  });
}

docs {
  # POST /quote-recaps — the renewal month is required (PAC-56 #16)

  Documents the one asymmetry in this field's contract, which is otherwise easy
  to "tidy" in the wrong direction:

  | surface | required? | why |
  |---|---|---|
  | `POST /quote-recaps` | **yes** | David asked for it on the form; a new recap should always record when the client's cover renews. |
  | `PATCH /quote-recaps/:id` | no | every migrated recap predates the field — requiring it would make all of them un-editable. |
  | Mongoose `QuoteRecap` | no | `required: true` would assert something false about thousands of existing documents and break the migration under `runValidators`. |

  So requiredness lives **only** in the create DTO. Deleting this request, or
  "fixing" the schema to require the field everywhere, breaks editing every
  recap imported from SmartSuite.

  - **Module:** `quote_recaps` · **Permission:** `quote_recaps:write`

  ## Also rejected
  SmartSuite's choice UUIDs (`0897f82f-de3a-4bbb-b973-c56bb1f4fecb` and the
  other eleven). They are for *reading* migrated data —
  `normalizeInsuranceMonth` maps them on every read — and accepting them on a
  write path would put a second vocabulary back into the collection, which is
  the mess `policyType` already had to be cleaned up from.

  ## Response `400`
  ```json
  {
    "message": "Validation failed",
    "errors": { "fieldErrors": { "insuranceRenewalMonth": ["Pick the renewal month"] } }
  }
  ```

  ## Run order
  Needs `createdLeadId` (Leads) and `quoteDocumentKey` (Presign + Upload Quote
  Document). Sends no `submissionToken`: a rejected request must not burn the
  idempotency key the earlier requests in this folder rely on.
}
